 "character": {
  "base": [
   "A diocese that has never been anyone's first choice and knows exactly what it is.",
   "A chancery small enough that the bishop signs the checks himself.",
   "One city, a ring of suburbs that took the parishes' money with them, and a long tail of towns with a church and a cemetery each.",
   "Founded by immigrants who built more churches than the diocese can now keep open.",
   "The priests know each other's cars. There is no anonymity here for anyone in a collar.",
   "A presbyterate that eats together once a month at a place that has been closing for ten years.",
   "The cathedral is the one building downtown that has not been sold to a developer.",
   "A place where a pastor's fortieth anniversary is front-page news.",
   "A diocese where the seminary sends men out and half of them come back to their home county.",
   "Farm country on one side of the see city and a university on the other, and a bishop who has to please both.",
   "The last three bishops came from elsewhere and left for elsewhere; the priests have stopped learning their habits.",
   "A Catholic hospital that outgrew the diocese that founded it and no longer answers the phone.",
   "A state capital's Catholic footprint: a lobbyist, a cathedral rector, and a great deal of lunch.",
   "A place the national Church notices only when something goes wrong.",
   "Two languages on most Sunday bulletins now, and an old guard that reads only one of them."
  ],
  "byNeed": {
   "critically_short": "There are pastors here with four churches and a driver's license the chancery prays over.",
   "stretched": "Every priest has a second job, and the second job is another parish.",
   "adequate": "There is a priest for every parish, barely, and no one to spare when one falls ill.",
   "deep_bench": "More men than posts, which is its own kind of politics."
  },
  "byFinancial": {
   "healthy": "The books balance, and the bishop has the rare luxury of choosing what to build.",
   "strained": "The annual appeal is a pleading letter now, and the pastors write it themselves.",
   "crisis": "A settlement, a bond, or both; the diocese is paying for something it would rather not name."
  },
  "byTension": {
   "one_voice": "The priests agree in public and mostly in private.",
